Subject: [PATCH 06/31] pine(L2): register chat.requestCancellation.enabled

A generic setting, default true, for whether Chat offers to cancel a running request. The Studio's extension sets it
false: its chats cannot be cancelled in v1, and the product ships no other chat.

diff --git a/src/vs/workbench/contrib/pine/browser/pine.contribution.ts b/src/vs/workbench/contrib/pine/browser/pine.contribution.ts
index 5d4d7d98088..227fc940ec7 100644
--- a/src/vs/workbench/contrib/pine/browser/pine.contribution.ts
+++ b/src/vs/workbench/contrib/pine/browser/pine.contribution.ts
@@ -23,6 +23,20 @@ Registry.as<IConfigurationRegistry>(ConfigurationExtensions.Configuration).regis
 	},
 }]);
 
+// Whether Chat offers to cancel a running request (Stop and its keybinding, chatExecuteActions.ts CancelAction). A product
+// whose chats cannot be cancelled turns it off; the Studio's extension does, and the product has
+// no other chat (pineShipsNoCopilot), so it is off for every chat there.
+Registry.as<IConfigurationRegistry>(ConfigurationExtensions.Configuration).registerConfiguration({
+	id: 'chat',
+	properties: {
+		'chat.requestCancellation.enabled': {
+			type: 'boolean',
+			default: true,
+			description: 'Controls whether a running chat request can be cancelled from Chat (Stop and its keybinding).',
+		},
+	},
+});
+
